Thanks all. Writing down what we know so far, proper RCA to follow.

What happened: orders-api 5.2 was deployed with a config map that no longer h=
ad PAYMENT_GATEWAY_URL. The app exits on start when that variable is missing,=
 so every pod crash looped and no orders could be placed for 17 minutes.
Impact: Full outage of order creation for 17 minutes. About 2,300 checkout at=
tempts failed. The monthly availability target of 99.9% was missed.

Timeline (UTC):
2026-03-12 16:40 orders-api 5.2 deploy started. None.
2026-03-12 16:42 Alert OrdersApiCrashLooping fired. On-call followed SOP-DEPL=
OY-001 and rolled back.
2026-03-12 16:45 The release owner, not knowing about the rollback, retried t=
he 5.2 deploy. Pods crash looped again.
2026-03-12 16:47 On-call read the logs and found "config error: PAYMENT_GATEW=
AY_URL is not set". Told the release owner to stop deploys.
2026-03-12 16:52 Rollout history showed the variable was dropped in the new r=
evision. Confirmed the cause with the release owner.
2026-03-12 16:55 Rollback to 5.1 started. Ran kubectl -n shop rollout undo de=
ploy/orders-api.
2026-03-12 16:59 Pods running and orders flowing again. Closed the incident. =
5.2 was redeployed at 19:30 with the config map mounted.

Root cause: The deploy did not mount the new config map, so PAYMENT_GATEWAY_U=
RL was missing and the app exited on start. Neither CI nor the readiness prob=
e checked for required config, so the bad revision reached every pod.
Fix: Rolled orders-api back to 5.1, then redeployed 5.2 later the same day wi=
th the new config map mounted.

Follow ups:
- Write SOP-DEPLOY-002 that reads the start up error before rolling back. (Sa=
ra Kim)
- Fail CI when a required config key is missing. (Orders team)
- Load config before the readiness probe reports ready. (Orders team)
- Post every rollback in the deploy channel. (SRE team)

